                <pb facs="0598" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5629: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-10T12:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                                1928—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 7:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>206. My 202, May 5, 3 p.m. About half of the delegates to the Conservative
                    Convention are still in dispute. Those definitely chosen seem to be fairly
                    evenly divided between the two parties [<hi rendition="#italic">factions?</hi>].
                    The decision in the contested cases will rest, according to the party statutes,
                    with the national Conservative directorate. Chamorro claims to control this body
                    but Cuadra Pasos asserts that each faction is sure of the votes of four members
                    and that the three remaining members are as yet doubtful. He intimated this
                    morning that unless an arrangement was reached before May 20 there would
                    probably be two conventions and General McCoy would be compelled to decide which
                    was the legal Conservative ticket. There have been frequent conferences this
                    week between the Conservative leaders in an effort to reach an agreement but
                    there is as yet no indication that either side will make any important
                    concession.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
